{"chunk_id": "7a5eb151c7f0", "text": "After the burning of the lac house, the citizens of Varanavata believe the Pandavas have perished in the fire set by Purochana at Duryodhana\u2019s command, and they bitterly condemn Dhritarashtra and the conspirators. In truth, the Pandavas escape through the secret tunnel prepared earlier. Exhausted and moving through darkness with their mother Kunti, they are carried by the powerful Bhima, who bears all his family as he forces a path through the forest. Meanwhile, Vidura\u2014aware of the plot through spies\u2014secretly sends a trusted agent who finds them near the Ganga and provides a specially prepared boat. Using coded words from Vidura as proof of loyalty, the agent ferries them across the river and urges secrecy. Back in the city, the townspeople discover the burned lac house and the bodies of a Nishada woman and her sons, mistakenly believing the Pandavas are dead, while the hidden escape tunnel is carefully concealed.\nVidura\u2019s agent guides the escaped Pandavas to a hidden boat, ferries them across the Ganga, while townspeople mourn, believing they perished in the lac house fire.\nThemes: escape and survival, political intrigue, loyalty of Vidura, deception and misdirection, brotherly protection", "vector": [0.009983986616134644, -0.01802491955459118, -0.0027113172691315413, -0.008709288202226162, -0.010486975312232971, 0.023123711347579956, -0.013938996009528637, -0.017170527949929237, -0.00331076979637146, -0.021428707987070084, 0.013484238646924496, 0.02131846360862255, 0.010190694592893124, 0.015158572234213352, -0.0007381190662272274, -0.0051401336677372456, 0.02765750326216221, -0.023812737315893173, 0.03698691353201866, -0.020794805139303207, -0.011120879091322422, -0.004485559184104204, 0.0017509872559458017, 0.017377234995365143, -0.03092348575592041, 0.009439656510949135, 0.010886610485613346, -0.02175944112241268, 0.005553549621254206, -0.008757520467042923, -0.00654230173677206, -0.00452001066878438, 